research/scan/SCAN.md:5:Savant r3 adds by a certified carry-lookahead scan over the {K, P, G} monoid. 2 certification records, 1 with decision_ok. The last is margin (decision_ok True, max |Δlogit| 0.5, min margin 1.5). At 4096 digits, 16 of 16 additions matched bigint on both schedules with every lookup on its row. Hillis–Steele model seconds on those 4096-digit records: median 3.52133 (min 3.5182, max 3.93983). At 100000 digits, 4 of 4 matched. Hillis–Steele model seconds: 115.676, 115.024, 115.223, 114.895. The L4 4096-digit addition has hs_exact True and bl_exact True, Hillis–Steele model seconds 34.5097. At 1000000 digits, hs_exact True, bl_exact True, hs_rounds 22, Hillis–Steele model seconds 1343.35. Settled ledger estimate 10.2727 USD against a cap of 18.2727 USD.
research/scan/SCAN.md:21:Registered before any Modal spend. Every count below was written by scan_report.py from results/algebra.json (scan_algebra.audit, seed 20261028).
research/scan/SCAN.md:43:Before the counted run. The smoke job scan-smoke-h100 measured full-chunk forwards of 4096 query tokens at D 0.158736 s, M 0.150481 s and S 0.16062 s, on NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3; unknown; GenuineIntel 6 143 unknown; avx512f=True, seed 20261028. The slower of those, times 914 forwards, extrapolates one 100000-digit Hillis–Steele addition to 146.807 s. That is above the registered 10 seconds, so prediction 4 is superseded: the Hillis–Steele model time at 100000 digits is under 183.509 seconds, which is 1.25 times that extrapolation. The smoke grid was not bitwise (max absolute logit difference 0.25, minimum margin 4.125, bound 0.5, decision margin, decision_ok True). Prediction 1's rule already covers that branch; it is not changed.
research/scan/SCAN.md:49:The order is the registered one: pairwise cosine at most that cap, then the sorted token ids, test pool before the train pool. K, P, and G are those three ids in increasing order. A triple is kept when its D, M, and S rows pass packed B=1 and the full invariance certificate on that Π has decision_ok true. That is prediction 1's predicate. D passes stored 44, which equals n_d_pass True. Records with passed true: 1. Distinct K texts 20. Stored D-miss signatures with count at least 2: 17. Missed rows across D failures: 766. Signatures seen once: 5 covering 5 missed rows.
